problem:
Problem description
- There are $$T$$ ordered planning periods indexed by $$t \in \mathcal{T}$$, representing the quarterly planning horizon for timber purchasing, storage, and sales.
- The company has one warehouse with storage capacity $$K$$ measured in timber volume units.
- Timber may be purchased at the beginning of each period, then sold in the same period or stored for later periods.
- The selling price, purchase price, and estimated maximum sales volume may vary by period.
- The storage charge per unit depends on the number of periods the timber remains in storage, with a base parameter $$a$$ and an age-dependent parameter $$b$$.
- The planning goal is to maximize total annual profit from timber purchases, storage, and sales.
- Inventory held in the warehouse must never exceed the storage capacity.
- Sales in each period must not exceed the estimated maximum sales volume for that period.
- Timber is not suitable for long-term storage, so all remaining inventory must be cleared by the end of the final period $$T$$.
- Inventory flow must remain consistent across periods, so timber available in each period can only come from current purchases and previously stored inventory.
- Storage cost must reflect the time each unit of timber spends in the warehouse.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_t$$: the quantity of timber purchased at the beginning of period $$t$$.
  - $$y_t$$: the quantity of timber sold during period $$t$$.
  - $$I_t$$: the inventory remaining at the end of period $$t$$.
  - $$z_{t,\tau}$$: the quantity purchased in period $$\tau$$ and sold in period $$t$$, used to track storage age and age-based holding cost, where $$\tau \le t$$.
  - $$Z$$: the total annual profit obtained by the plan.

Input Format
{
  "T": {
    "description": "Number of planning periods in the horizon.",
    "symbol": "$$T$$",
    "type": "integer"
  },
  "periods": {
    "description": "Ordered set of periods indexed by $$t \\in \\mathcal{T}$$.",
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{T}$$",
    "shape": "$$T$$",
    "type": "array"
  },
  "warehouse_capacity": {
    "description": "Maximum inventory that can be stored in the warehouse.",
    "symbol": "$$K$$",
    "type": "scalar"
  },
  "storage_cost_parameters": {
    "description": "Parameters governing per-unit storage charge as a function of storage age.",
    "fields": {
      "base_cost": {
        "symbol": "$$a$$",
        "type": "scalar"
      },
      "age_slope": {
        "symbol": "$$b$$",
        "type": "scalar"
      }
    }
  },
  "initial_inventory": {
    "description": "Inventory available before the first period begins.",
    "symbol": "$$I_0$$",
    "type": "scalar"
  },
  "final_inventory_requirement": {
    "description": "Required inventory remaining after the last period.",
    "symbol": "$$I_T$$",
    "type": "scalar"
  },
  "period_data": {
    "description": "Period-wise prices and sales limits.",
    "shape": "$$T$$",
    "type": "array of objects",
    "fields": {
      "purchase_price": {
        "description": "Unit purchase price in period $$t$$.",
        "symbol": "$$c_t^{\\mathrm{buy}}$$",
        "type": "scalar"
      },
      "sale_price": {
        "description": "Unit sale price in period $$t$$.",
        "symbol": "$$c_t^{\\mathrm{sell}}$$",
        "type": "scalar"
      },
      "max_sales_volume": {
        "description": "Maximum amount that can be sold in period $$t$$.",
        "symbol": "$$d_t$$",
        "type": "scalar"
      }
    }
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "purchase_plan": {
    "description": "Optimal quantity purchased at the beginning of each period.",
    "symbol": "$$x_t$$",
    "shape": "$$T$$",
    "type": "array"
  },
  "sales_plan": {
    "description": "Optimal quantity sold in each period.",
    "symbol": "$$y_t$$",
    "shape": "$$T$$",
    "type": "array"
  },
  "ending_inventory": {
    "description": "Inventory remaining at the end of each period.",
    "symbol": "$$I_t$$",
    "shape": "$$T$$",
    "type": "array"
  },
  "age_tracked_sales": {
    "description": "Optional age-tracked sales quantities for timber purchased in period $$\\tau$$ and sold in period $$t$$.",
    "symbol": "$$z_{t,\\tau}$$",
    "shape": "$$T \\times T$$",
    "type": "lower-triangular array"
  },
  "objective_value": {
    "description": "Maximum total annual profit achieved by the plan.",
    "symbol": "$$Z$$",
    "type": "scalar"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "T": 4,
  "periods": ["Winter", "Spring", "Summer", "Autumn"],
  "warehouse_capacity": 200000,
  "storage_cost_parameters": {
    "base_cost": 70,
    "age_slope": 100
  },
  "initial_inventory": 0,
  "final_inventory_requirement": 0,
  "period_data": [
    {
      "period": "Winter",
      "purchase_price": 410,
      "sale_price": 425,
      "max_sales_volume": 100
    },
    {
      "period": "Spring",
      "purchase_price": 430,
      "sale_price": 440,
      "max_sales_volume": 140
    },
    {
      "period": "Summer",
      "purchase_price": 460,
      "sale_price": 465,
      "max_sales_volume": 200
    },
    {
      "period": "Autumn",
      "purchase_price": 450,
      "sale_price": 455,
      "max_sales_volume": 160
    }
  ]
}
